{"slug":"/students/subjects/mathematics/algebraic-foundations/quadratic-equations/","source":"students/subjects/mathematics/algebraic-foundations/quadratic-equations.html","area":"students","kind":"content","title":"Mathematics - Quadratic Equation","description":"","subject":"mathematics","body":"<div class=\"flex flex-col min-h-screen\">\n        <!-- Header -->\n        <header class=\"bg-white shadow-sm sticky top-0 z-40\">\n            <div class=\"max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-3\">\n                <div class=\"flex items-center justify-between\">\n                    <a href=\"/students/subjects/mathematics/algebraic-foundations/\" class=\"flex items-center gap-3 text-gray-600 hover:text-gray-900\">\n                        <span class=\"mi -arrow-left\" data-mi=\"arrow_back\">arrow_back</span>\n                        <span class=\"font-semibold text-lg\">Mastering Quadratic Equations</span>\n                    </a>\n                    <div class=\"flex items-center gap-4\">\n                        <div class=\"text-sm text-gray-500\">\n                            <span>Progress:</span>\n                            <div class=\"w-32 bg-gray-200 rounded-full h-2.5 inline-block ml-2\">\n                                <div class=\"bg-blue-600 h-2.5 rounded-full\" style=\"width: 0%\"></div>\n                            </div>\n                        </div>\n                        <img src=\"/site/assets/images/logo.png\" alt=\"logo\" class=\"h-10 w-auto\">\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </header>\n\n        <!-- Main Content -->\n        <main class=\"flex-grow max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-8 w-full\">\n            <div class=\"grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-8\">\n                <!-- Left Sidebar: Learning Steps -->\n                <aside class=\"lg:col-span-1\">\n                    <div class=\"bg-white p-5 rounded-xl shadow-sm sticky top-24\">\n                        <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-lg mb-4\">Tools</h3>\n                        <p>Sub-topics</p>\n                        <ul class=\"space-y-2\">\n                            <li><a href=\"#solving\" class=\"flex items-center gap-3 p-2 rounded-md hover:bg-blue-50 text-gray-700 font-medium\"><span class=\"mi -calculator w-5 text-center text-blue-500\" data-mi=\"calculate\">calculate</span><span>Solving Equations</span></a></li>\n                            <li><a href=\"#forming\" class=\"flex items-center gap-3 p-2 rounded-md hover:bg-blue-50 text-gray-700 font-medium\"><span class=\"mi -cogs w-5 text-center text-green-500\" data-mi=\"settings\">settings</span><span>Forming &amp; Applications</span></a></li>\n                            <li><a href=\"#graphs\" class=\"flex items-center gap-3 p-2 rounded-md hover:bg-blue-50 text-gray-700 font-medium\"><span class=\"mi -chart-line w-5 text-center text-purple-500\" data-mi=\"show_chart\">show_chart</span><span>Graphs &amp; Functions</span></a></li>\n                        </ul>\n                        <p>Resources</p>\n                        <ul class=\"space-y-2\">\n                            <li><a href=\"#resources\" class=\"flex items-center gap-3 p-2 rounded-md hover:bg-blue-50 text-gray-700 font-medium\"><span class=\"mi -robot w-5 text-center text-green-500\" data-mi=\"smart_toy\">smart_toy</span><span>Interactive Solver</span></a></li>\n                            <li><a href=\"#resources\" class=\"flex items-center gap-3 p-2 rounded-md hover:bg-blue-50 text-gray-700 font-medium\"><span class=\"mi -project-diagram w-5 text-center text-purple-500\" data-mi=\"schema\">schema</span><span>Graph Visualizer</span></a></li>\n                        </ul>\n                    </div>\n                </aside>\n\n                <!-- Right Content Area -->\n                <div class=\"lg:col-span-3\">\n                    <div class=\"space-y-8\" id=\"learning-content\">\n                        <!-- Section 1: Solving Quadratic Equations -->\n                        <div id=\"solving\" data-step=\"0\" class=\"learning-step bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-xl shadow-sm p-6 scroll-mt-24\">\n                            <h2 class=\"text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\"><span class=\"mi -calculator text-blue-500 mr-3\" data-mi=\"calculate\">calculate</span>Solving Quadratic Equations</h2>\n                            <p class=\"text-gray-600 mb-6\">A quadratic equation is any equation that can be written as <code class=\"font-mono bg-gray-100 p-1 rounded text-sm\">ax² + bx + c = 0</code>. \"Solving\" it means finding the values of 'x' that make the equation true. Let's explore the common methods.</p>\n                            \n                            <div class=\"space-y-4\" id=\"solving-methods\">\n                                <!-- Accordion sections will be dynamically populated -->\n                            </div>\n                        </div>\n\n                        <!-- Section 2: Forming Equations & Applications -->\n                        <div id=\"forming\" data-step=\"1\" class=\"learning-step bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-xl shadow-sm p-6 scroll-mt-24\">\n                            <h2 class=\"text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\"><span class=\"mi -cogs text-green-500 mr-3\" data-mi=\"settings\">settings</span>Forming &amp; Applying Equations</h2>\n                            <div class=\"space-y-4\">\n                              <div>\n                                <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-lg text-gray-700\">Forming an Equation from Given Roots</h3>\n                                <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mt-1\"><strong>The Big Idea:</strong> This is factorization in reverse. If you know the roots, you can rebuild the equation.</p>\n                                <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mt-2\">If the roots are <code class=\"font-mono bg-gray-100\">α</code> and <code class=\"font-mono bg-gray-100\">β</code>, the equation is <code class=\"font-mono bg-gray-100\">x² - (sum of roots)x + (product of roots) = 0</code>. <br><strong>Example:</strong> If roots are 4 and -5, the Sum = -1 and the Product = -20. The equation is <code class=\"font-mono bg-gray-100\">x² - (-1)x + (-20) = 0</code>, which simplifies to <code class=\"font-mono bg-gray-100\">x² + x - 20 = 0</code>.</p>\n                              </div>\n                              <div class=\"pt-4 border-t\">\n                                <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-lg text-gray-700\">Application in Practical Problems</h3>\n                                <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mt-1\"><strong>The Big Idea:</strong> Translate a real-world word problem into a quadratic equation to solve it.</p>\n                                <div class=\"mt-2 bg-yellow-50 border-l-4 border-yellow-400 p-3\">\n                                  <h4 class=\"font-semibold\">How to Translate Word Problems:</h4>\n                                  <ul class=\"list-disc list-inside pl-2 mt-1\">\n                                    <li><strong>Identify the unknown:</strong> Call it 'x' or another variable (like 'w' for width).</li>\n                                    <li><strong>Formulate the equation:</strong> Use the information given (e.g., area = length × width) to write an equation.</li>\n                                    <li><strong>Solve:</strong> Use one of the methods above to find the value of your unknown.</li>\n                                    <li><strong>Check your answer:</strong> Does the solution make sense in the real world? (e.g., length cannot be negative).</li>\n                                  </ul>\n                                </div>\n                              </div>\n                            </div>\n                        </div>\n\n                        <!-- Section 3: Graphs -->\n                        <div id=\"graphs\" data-step=\"2\" class=\"learning-step bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-xl shadow-sm p-6 scroll-mt-24\">\n                            <h2 class=\"text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\"><span class=\"mi -chart-line text-purple-500 mr-3\" data-mi=\"show_chart\">show_chart</span>Graphs of Quadratic Functions</h2>\n                            <p class=\"text-gray-600 mb-4\">Visualizing quadratic equations is a powerful way to understand them. When you plot <code class=\"font-mono bg-gray-100 text-sm\">y = ax² + bx + c</code>, you get a special U-shaped curve.</p>\n                            \n                            <div class=\"space-y-6\">\n                              <div>\n                                <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-lg text-gray-700\">What is a Parabola?</h3>\n                                <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mt-1\">A <strong>parabola</strong> is the name for the symmetrical, U-shaped curve created by a quadratic equation. It can open upwards (like a smile) if 'a' is positive, or downwards (like a frown) if 'a' is negative.</p>\n                              </div>\n\n                              <div>\n                                <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-lg text-gray-700\">Drawing the Graph (Step-by-Step)</h3>\n                                <ol class=\"list-decimal list-inside space-y-1 text-gray-600 text-sm mt-1\">\n                                  <li><strong>Create a Table of Values:</strong> Choose several x-values and plug them into the equation to find the corresponding y-values.</li>\n                                  <li><strong>Plot the Points:</strong> Mark these (x, y) coordinate pairs on your graph paper.</li>\n                                  <li><strong>Draw the Curve:</strong> Connect the points with a smooth, continuous curve to form your parabola.</li>\n                                </ol>\n                              </div>\n\n                              <div>\n                                <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-lg text-gray-700\">Finding Roots from the Graph</h3>\n                                <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mt-1\">The \"roots\" or \"solutions\" are simply the x-values where the parabola intersects the x-axis (the horizontal line). Think of it as where the curve hits the ground.</p>\n                                <div class=\"mt-3 bg-gray-50 p-4 rounded-lg border\">\n                                  <div class=\"mt-4\">\n                                    <img src=\"/site/assets/images/mathematics/quadratic-roots.svg\" alt=\"Graph showing different types of quadratic roots: two real roots (crosses the x-axis at two points), one real root (touches the x-axis at one point), and no real roots (doesn't cross the x-axis)\" class=\"w-full max-w-2xl mx-auto border border-gray-200 rounded-lg\">\n                                  </div>\n                                  <p class=\"text-xs text-gray-500 mt-2\">\n                                    <strong>Interactive Demo:</strong> Drag the points A and B to change the equation and see how the roots change. \n                                    The x-coordinates where the parabola crosses the x-axis are the roots.\n                                  </p>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"bg-blue-50 p-3 rounded-lg mt-3\">\n                                  <p class=\"text-sm\"><strong>Key Points:</strong></p>\n                                  <ul class=\"list-disc list-inside text-sm space-y-1 mt-1\">\n                                    <li>A parabola can cross the x-axis 0, 1, or 2 times</li>\n                                    <li>Two crossings = two real roots (most common)</li>\n                                    <li>One crossing = one repeated root</li>\n                                    <li>No crossing = no real roots (complex roots)</li>\n                                  </ul>\n                                </div>\n                              </div>\n\n                              <div class=\"mt-6\">\n                                <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-lg text-gray-700\">Solving a System of Equations Graphically</h3>\n                                <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mt-1\">To solve a pair of equations like <code class=\"font-mono bg-gray-100\">y = ax² + bx + c</code> (a curve) and <code class=\"font-mono bg-gray-100\">y = mx + k</code> (a straight line), draw both on the same graph. The points where the line and the parabola cross are the solutions.</p>\n                                <div class=\"mt-3 bg-gray-50 p-4 rounded-lg border\">\n                                  <div class=\"mt-4\">\n                                    <img src=\"/site/assets/images/mathematics/quadratic-linear-intersection.svg\" alt=\"Graph showing a parabola intersecting with a straight line at two points, demonstrating the solution to a system of equations\" class=\"w-full max-w-2xl mx-auto border border-gray-200 rounded-lg\">\n                                  </div>\n                                  <p class=\"text-xs text-gray-500 mt-2\">\n                                    <strong>Interactive Demo:</strong> Drag points to modify both the parabola and the line. \n                                    The intersection points (if any) are the solutions to both equations.\n                                  </p>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"bg-blue-50 p-3 rounded-lg mt-3\">\n                                  <p class=\"text-sm\"><strong>Possible Outcomes:</strong></p>\n                                  <ul class=\"list-disc list-inside text-sm space-y-1 mt-1\">\n                                    <li>Two intersections = two solutions</li>\n                                    <li>One intersection = one solution (line touches the parabola)</li>\n                                    <li>No intersections = no solutions (line doesn't meet the parabola)</li>\n                                  </ul>\n                                </div>\n                              </div>\n\n                              <div class=\"mt-6\">\n                                <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-lg text-gray-700\">Finding the Gradient with a Tangent</h3>\n                                <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mt-1\">A <strong>tangent</strong> is a straight line that \"just kisses\" the curve at a single point without crossing through it. The slope (or gradient) of this tangent line tells you how steep the curve is at that exact point.</p>\n                                <div class=\"mt-3 bg-gray-50 p-4 rounded-lg border\">\n                                  <div class=\"mt-4\">\n                                    <img src=\"/site/assets/images/mathematics/quadratic-features.svg\" alt=\"Graph of a parabola with labeled key features: vertex, axis of symmetry, y-intercept, and direction of opening\" class=\"w-full max-w-2xl mx-auto border border-gray-200 rounded-lg\">\n                                  </div>\n                                  <p class=\"text-xs text-gray-500 mt-2\">\n                                    <strong>Interactive Demo:</strong> Move point A along the curve to see how the tangent line changes. \n                                    The slope of this line gives you the gradient of the curve at that point.\n                                  </p>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"bg-blue-50 p-3 rounded-lg mt-3\">\n                                  <p class=\"text-sm\"><strong>How to Find the Gradient:</strong></p>\n                                  <ol class=\"list-decimal list-inside text-sm space-y-1 mt-1\">\n                                    <li>Draw the tangent line at your chosen point</li>\n                                    <li>Pick two points on your tangent line (not too close together)</li>\n                                    <li>Calculate the gradient using: <code class=\"font-mono bg-gray-100\">rise ÷ run</code> or <code class=\"font-mono bg-gray-100\">(y₂-y₁)/(x₂-x₁)</code></li>\n                                  </ol>\n                                </div>\n                              </div>\n                            </div>\n                        </div>\n\n                        <!-- Resources Section -->\n                        <div id=\"resources\" data-step=\"3\" class=\"learning-step space-y-8 scroll-mt-24\">\n                            <h2 class=\"text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4\">Resources</h2>\n                            <!-- Interactive Solver -->\n                            <div class=\"bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-xl shadow-sm p-6\">\n                                <h3 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4\">Interactive Solver</h3>\n                                <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-500 mb-4\">Enter the coefficients for <code class=\"font-mono\">ax² + bx + c = 0</code></p>\n                                <div class=\"grid grid-cols-3 gap-3 mb-4\">\n                                    <div>\n                                        <label for=\"coeff-a\" class=\"font-medium text-sm\">a</label>\n                                        <input type=\"number\" id=\"coeff-a\" value=\"1\" class=\"w-full mt-1 p-2 border rounded-md text-center\">\n                                    </div>\n                                    <div>\n                                        <label for=\"coeff-b\" class=\"font-medium text-sm\">b</label>\n                                        <input type=\"number\" id=\"coeff-b\" value=\"-5\" class=\"w-full mt-1 p-2 border rounded-md text-center\">\n                                    </div>\n                                    <div>\n                                        <label for=\"coeff-c\" class=\"font-medium text-sm\">c</label>\n                                        <input type=\"number\" id=\"coeff-c\" value=\"6\" class=\"w-full mt-1 p-2 border rounded-md text-center\">\n                                    </div>\n                                </div>\n                                <button id=\"solve-btn\" class=\"w-full bg-blue-600 text-white font-semibold py-2 rounded-md hover:bg-blue-700 transition\">Solve</button>\n                                <div id=\"solver-output\" class=\"mt-4 pt-4 border-t\">\n                                    <!-- Output will be rendered here -->\n                                </div>\n                            </div>\n                            \n                            <!-- Graph Visualizer -->\n                            <div class=\"bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-xl shadow-sm p-6\">\n                                <h3 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4\">Graph Visualizer</h3>\n                                <canvas id=\"quadratic-chart\" height=\"200\"></canvas>\n                            </div>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </main>\n\n        <!-- Footer Navigation -->\n        <footer class=\"bg-white/80 backdrop-blur-sm border-t border-gray-200 sticky bottom-0 z-40\">\n            <div class=\"max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-3\">\n                <div class=\"flex justify-between items-center\">\n                    <button id=\"prev-btn\" class=\"flex items-center gap-2 px-4 py-2 text-gray-600 font-semibold rounded-lg hover:bg-gray-200 disabled:opacity-50 disabled:cursor-not-allowed\">\n                        <span class=\"mi -arrow-left\" data-mi=\"arrow_back\">arrow_back</span>\n                        <span>Previous</span>\n                    </button>\n                    <button id=\"next-btn\" class=\"flex items-center gap-2 px-4 py-2 bg-blue-600 text-white font-semibold rounded-lg hover:bg-blue-700 disabled:opacity-50 disabled:cursor-not-allowed\">\n                        <span>Next</span>\n                        <span class=\"mi -arrow-right\" data-mi=\"arrow_forward\">arrow_forward</span>\n                    </button>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </footer>\n    </div>\n\n    \n<!-- Topic Quiz System -->","bodyClass":"bg-gray-100 font-inter","bodyStyle":"","css":[],"quiz":null,"tracker":null,"links":["#solving","#forming","#graphs","#resources"]}